  "title": "# Build: window-resize-fix (Current profile) - URGENT bug fix ## Brett said (verbatim, Nov 3 2026, …",
  "asked": "# Build: window-resize-fix (Current profile) - URGENT bug fix ## Brett said (verbatim, Nov 3 2026, voice) \"Why can't I resize terminal? All floating windows need to be resizable. And also, I selected dialog for the terminal settings in its settings, but it doesn't open.\" Assigned agent: whoever is free (router if on main; else **Landin' Lenny**; record who). Register in the `current` profile (id `window-resize-fix`) + banner entry. Fix right away, tell after. ## Bug 1: floating windows can't be resized (phone at least) - The window engine got resize from all 8 edges/corners in windows-terminal s6 (refactor-all s17-s23, report `_claude/memory/docs/rebuilds/windows-terminal-fable.md`). Brett can't resize the Terminal floating window now. Find why on the live console (console.amberxai.com, his phone + desktop): handles missing/too small for touch, pointer events not wired for touch (need pointer events + touch-action none on handles), a later change (one-look, xlayout/dock engine #245/#252, compact frame, Molly chrome) overriding the window host, or the Terminal opening in a non-window host. - Fix in the framework window host so EVERY floating window in every app is resizable: 8 edges + corners, big enough touch targets on phones (invisible hit area ~16-24 px, visible grip in the corner), min/max size from tokens, remembers size per window, double-tap title = maximize/restore. CI test: every floating window exposes resize handles. ## Bug 2: Terminal settings placement 'dialog' does nothing - Terminal's own setting for where its settings open: Brett picked 'dialog' and tapping the gear no longer opens anything (before, it opened the main settings page). Fix so 'dialog' opens the Terminal settings in a pop-up dialog and the main-page option still works. Check every plugin that has this option for the same bug. Coordinate with the queued `plugin-settings-placement` build only via its contract; this is the quick fix for the existing option. ## Done Tests (resize via pointer + touch, dialog placement), phone + desktop before/after screenshots, UI Review item, report `_claude/builds/reports/window-resize-fix.md`, THREADS, PR, steps through the store. Commits clean and professional. ## Addendum 1 (Brett, Nov 3 2026, voice): \"Run that right here, right now, and merge it, deploy it.\" Brett's explicit order for THIS build only: when tests pass, merge the PR into main yourself right away (do NOT wait for UI Review; still submit the UI Review item for the record, marked 'merged on Brett's order'), then make sure the console (axf-console), axHub web, AmberX web and Molly redeploy with it (CI deploy on main / Coolify redeploy), and confirm the live console has the fix. Keep it small and fast: fix the two bugs, no extras. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
